  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing Protection Risks and Fostering Social Cohesion in Rohingya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Identified protection risks and needs are addressed by increasing refugees&apos; capacity in self -protection through community -based initiatives and facilitation of meaningful access to services. Specifically, prevention of Gender Based Violence (GBV) and trafficking, provision of Non Food Items (NFIs), Social Cohesion, Public Lighting and Protection Monitoring linked to advocacy. To ensure safety, well -being and dignity of crisis -affected Rohingya refugee and host community populations by mitigating, preventing and protecting against pervasive gender -based violence, trafficking in persons, and other forms of harm faced by vulnerable groups in Cox&apos;s Bazar District.</narrative>
  </description>
